legend: {
  shape: text
  label: |md
    ## Database Relationship
    ### 1:N Relationships
    - **Departments → Major** (1:N): One department has many major
    - **Departments → Professors** (1:N): One department has many professors
    - **Majors → Students** (1:N): One major has many student
    - **Sections → Timetables** (1:N): Each section has many lessons
    - **Semesters → Sections** (1:N): There are many classes each semester.
    - **Major_courses → Sections** (1:N): Each major_course will have many classes.
    - **Professors → Sections** (1:N): Each professor is in charge of many class.

    ### M:N Relationships
    - **Courses ↔ Majors** (M:N): Each major has many courses and each course is part of the curriculum of many majors.
    - **Courses ↔ Courses** (M:N): Each course can requires one or more prerequisite courses.
    - **Students ↔ Sections** (M:N): Each student studies in many classes and each class has many students.

    ### Notes
    - All tables have a create time and an update time.
  |
}
